course: dictionary
lesson: 7563
title: Words from church life
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: A presbyter is a word from church life, and you may meet it in Bible study or in the names of some churches. It means an elder, a leader who helps look after a local church.
explain: «Presbyterian churches are led by elected elders, called presbyters.» The word called tells you that presbyter is another name for the elders. Elected is a clue too: the elders are chosen by the people of the church.
explain: In some churches a presbyter is a priest, but in Presbyterian churches it means an elder who helps lead the congregation. The phrase «the presbyters of the church» means the leaders of that church, so context gives you the meaning.
fact: A presbyter is an elder or leader of a local church.
fact: «Presbyterian churches are led by elected elders, called presbyters.»
fact: In some churches a presbyter is a priest; in Presbyterian churches a presbyter is an elder who helps lead the congregation.
fact: Presbyter comes from a Greek word meaning elder.
fact: The Presbyterian Church is named after presbyters, the elders who lead it together.
exercise: «Presbyterian churches are led by elected elders, called presbyters.» In this sentence, what are presbyters? | Bells that ring for Sunday | *Elders who help lead the church | Hymn books | Church towers
exercise: In Presbyterian churches, what does a presbyter do? | Sings alone in the choir | Rings the church bell | Sells tickets at the door | *Helps lead the congregation as an elder
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as presbyter? | *Elder | Steeple | Choirboy | Sermon
test: «The presbyters of the church met on Sunday to pray together.» What does presbyters mean here? | Visitors from far away | *Church leaders, or elders | Church bells | Stained glass windows
test: The word presbyter comes from a Greek word meaning what? | Bell | Steeple | Choir | *Elder
exam: Lena says a presbyter is a kind of bell. Is she right? | *No, a presbyter is an elder who helps lead a church | No, a presbyter is only a Bible story | Yes, it rings on Sundays | Yes, it is a bell in the tower
